WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
Sometimes, we can feel like staying away or getting angry even when what makes us feel

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.640
that way isn't right near us.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.480
For example, Mike might want to stay away in gym class when Mr. Ramos is there, but

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:16.199
he might also want to stay away when he sees someone from gym class and thinks about Mr.

00:00:16.199 --> 00:00:17.199
Ramos.

00:00:17.199 --> 00:00:19.519
We call these reminders triggers.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.879
We want to show you how triggers work.

00:00:21.879 --> 00:00:23.760
And the picture above is Dave.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.600
Dave is usually an easygoing kid who gets along with everyone.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.240
But recently, Dave's grandfather, who helped raise him, died.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:35.679
Since then, Dave doesn't want to talk much with his friends.

00:00:35.679 --> 00:00:37.719
He likes to stay in his room.

00:00:37.719 --> 00:00:42.079
He misses watching old Simpson shows with his grandfather playing cards and talking

00:00:42.079 --> 00:00:43.640
about his day.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:48.040
When his mom makes him come out of his room, he gets angry and they often argue when he

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.680
has to go to school or eat dinner.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:53.040
He just wants to be left alone.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.840
Even when he's in his room, he feels sad most of the time.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.840
Now answer some true or false questions about Dave.

